#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Supervises a bundled moq-relay, so KASTR can BE the relay as well as use one.

moq-relay is the upstream Rust server (kixelated/moq). Speaking moq-lite over
QUIC/WebTransport is not something to reimplement, so the official binary is
bundled and driven here -- the same approach as ffmpeg for RTSP.

Configuration goes through a generated relay.toml rather than CLI flags: the
public-access prefix for an unauthenticated relay is the empty string, and an
empty argv entry is unreliable to pass through a Windows shell.

Secured mode (0.7.0; 0.16.0 per-session auth): the relay POSTs every session
event to the token service on relay-port+1, which verifies KASTR's HS256
tokens (signed with a locally generated JWK) and answers a grant. Room records
-- locked {slug, salt, hash}, kept and plain rooms -- are saved in
relay-auth.json; a room that is not kept is forgotten ROOM_TTL after its last
use. Room listing and stats stay public (subscribe-only) so the pre-join
screen needs no token.

Access codes (0.10.0): relay-wide VIEWER, PUBLISHER, ADMIN and FEDERATION
codes, kept hashed (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256) in relay-auth.json, decide the ROLE of
a token; the room decides its paths. With codes configured every room -- main
included -- refuses to mint without one. A viewer token can subscribe to the
room and announce the presence-class kinds (VIEWER_KINDS) but carries no
publish claim on media; the relay drops such an announce and keeps the
session. Every control path lives under the '~' namespace (NS). Room codes
remain an extra per-room lock. Without codes a secured relay mints for any
room code and status() says so (`legacy`). The relay control plane
(GUARDED_POSTS) answers the machine itself only.

Endpoints (wired up by kastr_serve; the main ones):
    GET  /api/relay/status  -> {running, url, port, bindAll, fingerprint, codes, legacy, federation, ...}
    POST /api/relay/start   {"port":4443,"lan":true,"secured":true}   (lan = bind all interfaces; persists the shape)
    POST /api/relay/stop
    GET  /api/relay/codes   -> which codes are set;  POST {"viewer"|"publisher"|"federation"|"admin": "..."|""|null}  ("" clears, null keeps)
    GET  /api/relay/cluster -> {"connect","master","hasCode"};  POST {connect?, code?, master?}
    POST /api/relay/rotate  -> new signing key (every token dies), relay restarted
    GET  /api/relay/rooms   -> {"rooms":[...], "closed":{slug:ts_ms}, "groups":{gid:{name,order,rooms}}}
    POST /api/relay/rooms/close {"slug"}  -> operator close: record, chat and attachments gone
    POST /api/relay/rooms/group {"op":"create|rename|delete|assign",...}  (operator)
    GET  /api/relay/vehicles -> {"vehicles":[{id,name,host,created,lastUsed,lastRoom,revoked}], "spoke"}  (hub; never a key)
    POST /api/relay/vehicles {"op":"create","name"} -> {"ok","vehicle","key"} (the key ONCE); {"op":"revoke|delete","id"}
    GET  /api/relay/links   0.21.77: the relay mesh (hub) -- {nodes, links, hubCost}; POST {a, b, mode, cost, addr} | {hubCost}
                            0.21.78: + POST {node, kind: hub|standby, cost} (one spoke's link); links carry bps {fwd, back}
Token service (its own listener, relay-port+1):
    GET  /api/auth          -> {"app":"KASTR","secured":true,"codes","legacy","federation","kid","ns","web","https",...}
    GET  /api/rooms         -> {"rooms":[...],"groups":{...}}
    POST /api/room          {"slug","salt"?,"hash"?,"roomKey"?,"code"?,"access"?,"persistent"?,"creator"?,"rekey"?,"plain"?}
    POST /api/token         {"room","code","roomCode"?,"host"?} -> {"ok":true,"role","exp","ns",tokens:{member,registry}}
                            with "host" (<slug>-<4 hex>) the member token's puts are scoped to that host's own
                            paths (+ its ~state/<room>/<host> track); {"federation":"<code>"} -> a relay token
    POST /api/vehicle       0.21.63: {"key","room","name"?,"roomCode"?} -> {"ok","room","host","op","prefix","relay","jwt",
                            "connect","exp","refreshEvery","created"} -- a publish-only token for <room>/<host>; the room
                            is made plain when missing and touched by every call (docs/vehicle-api.md)
    POST /api/session       the relay's per-session auth callback (loopback only)
    POST /api/invite        0.21.75: {room, ttl: 3600|86400|604800, by?} with Bearer = a member token of that room ->
                            {ok, id, token, exp} -- a room invite link's secret (made at the hub; only its sha256 is kept)
    POST /api/invite/revoke 0.21.75: {room, id | all: true, roomKey?} (the room's creator or an admin)
    GET  /api/invites?room= 0.21.75: the room's live invite links {id, by, created, exp, uses} (never a secret); POST
                            {room, roomKey?} answers the same for the creator (the roomKey never rides a URL)
                            /api/token {room, invite, host} redeems one: no access code, no room code, a publisher
    POST /api/xshare        0.21.41: list a room's stream in other rooms (Bearer = member token of the stream's room)
                            {path, to:[slug], tokens:{slug: member token}, label?, kind?, by?, stop?}
    GET  /api/xshare?room=  0.21.41: the live listings into a room (Bearer / ?jwt= member token; loopback page: none)
    GET  /api/rooms/board?room=  0.21.63: the room board {ok, room, pins, spots, grids, ver} (member token of that room;
                            loopback: none)
    POST /api/rooms/board   0.21.63: {room, op: pin|unpin|spot|unspot, path|target, from?, label?, kind?, by?, ts?,
                            tokens?: {<from room>: member token}} with Bearer = a PUBLISHER member token for <room>
                            0.21.64: + op grid {path, rects: {<member path>: [x,y,w,h] of 24}, gap} | gridHide {path,
                            member} | gridShow {path, member} | gridReset {path} -- the room's own layout of a camera grid
                            0.21.65: op grid may carry `slots` [{rect, cams: [member path], cycle: {mode, every, hold}}]
                            + `sens` (the grid builder: several cameras per spot, cycling); op split | unsplit {path} --
                            a grid's camera shown on its own in this room (`split` in the reply)
    0.21.84 -- the stream library (lib/<host>/<op>/<leaf>.hang; scratchpad API.md has the bodies):
    POST /api/token         {library: true, code, host} -> a library publisher token (publishes under lib/<host>)
    POST /api/library       a publisher's heartbeat {rows, stop?, moved?, stills?, box?, site?} (Bearer = that token)
    GET  /api/library       ?since=<ver>&paths=<a,b> -> the catalogue (member / library viewer token; loopback page: none)
    GET  /api/library/still ?path=&v= -> image/jpeg
    POST /api/library/token Bearer = a member token -> a library viewer token (the page's library connection)
    POST /api/library/admin {op: hide|unhide|label|site|remove, ...} (admins; the hub keeps it; fail closed when dark)
    GET|POST /api/relay/library  the Relay page: the fleet switch {on}, pre-flight, sites, entries (this machine only)
"""
import base64
import hashlib
import hmac
import json
import kastr_ua  # noqa: F401  -- 0.21.64: every request says KASTR (Cloudflare refuses Python-urllib)
import os
import random
